• Bucket Array: The foundation of a HashMap is a plain array of Node objects called table, where each index represents a bucket. The default initial capacity is 16, and the array size is always a power of two.
• Node Object: Each entry is stored as a Node containing four components:
	• hash: The precomputed hash code of the key.
	• key: The key object.
	• value: The associated value.
	• next: A reference to the next Node in case of a collision (forms a linked list).
• Null Handling: A HashMap permits one null key and multiple null values.
